sec.p:
The unsegregated ranking was calculated based on the PPSSI and total synapse count of neuron k:
(4)
unsegregated score k=log10⁡(Wk)⋅(1−PPSSIk) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle _{k}=\log _{10}\left(W_{k}\right) \cdot\left(1-P P S S I_{k}\right)$$\end{document}
where PPSSIk is the PPSSI of neuron k and Wk is the total synapse count of neuron k. This allows us to extract neurons with many inputs and outputs and highly unsegregated synapses. The segregated ranking was also calculated in the same way, using the following score:
(5)
segregated score k=log10⁡(Wk)⋅ PPSSI k \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \text { segregated score }_{k}=\log _{10}\left(W_{k}\right) \cdot \text { PPSSI }_{k} \tag{5} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
